Keep all examples using made-up project names.

Record the user's decisions in `doc/design/future-architecture.md` and add a detailed Homebrew section.

## Record
- app name `agentic-status-bar`, short form and CLI name `asb`;
- minimum macOS 14;
- the hook moves to Swift (no shell left);
- the SwiftBar plugin is removed once the Swift migration is complete;
- atm's JSON becomes a stable contract at some point, and we live with drift until then.

## Homebrew section
From the start vs later (own tap vs homebrew/cask, cask vs formula for the CLI, notability rules, `auto_updates` with Sparkle, release automation), with 'later' as the recommendation.

Update the recommendation and open questions.

Add a section to `doc/design/future-architecture.md` on Swift vs alternatives and the cross-platform question.

## Answer
- can Swift do everything for the macOS app or does any part need another language;
- alternatives (Objective-C, Rust/Tauri, Go, .NET/Avalonia, Electron, Kotlin Compose, Flutter) and reasons to prefer any of them;
- can Rust/Tauri give one implementation for macOS, Windows and Linux (tray differences, GNOME tray, WSL, process checks, terminal focus, notifications), and at what effort;
- and a phased path that solidifies on Swift first and moves to a cross-platform stack later, with what to do now to keep that cheap.

Update the recommendation and open questions.

`Sources/ASBCore/Processes.swift`: a `ProcessInspector` protocol with a fake and a libproc implementation.

## Change
- `protocol ProcessInspector { func snapshot() -> [Int32: ProcessInfo] }` with `ProcessInfo {pid, ppid, start (epoch seconds), comm, args (optional)}`;
- a `FakeProcessInspector` for tests;
- and a macOS implementation using libproc (`proc_listallpids`, `proc_pidinfo` `PROC_PIDTBSDINFO` for `ppid`, start time and `comm`) in a file compiled only on macOS (`#if os(macOS)`) so `ASBCore` stays portable.
- Also a helper converting the shell era's `procStart` strings ('Mon Oct 19 09:12:03 2026', local time, extra spaces allowed) to epoch seconds.

## Tests
- the fake;
- the real inspector finds the test process itself with a plausible start time and its parent.

`Sources/ASBCore/MenuModel.swift` builds the `Snapshot` from reconciled sessions.

## Header
Header priority: warning if invalid files, then waiting, idle, uncertain, busy count over unmuted sessions; all muted → muted symbol without count; none → none symbol.

## Rows
- sorted by rank (waiting 0, idle 1, uncertain 2, busy/subagents 3, muted 5) then `since`;
- label = project (`cwd` basename or 'unknown') + ' — ' + title (herdr terminal title, then `sessionName`, then `promptPreview`), '|' replaced by '│', fitted to 48 characters with '…' or padded, `:name:` broken with a zero-width space;
- word (permission, question, idle, no activity, waiting on N subagent(s), working);
- durations (s, m, h, d);
- mute text ('muted today' or 'muted until HH:MM');
- subagent rows sorted by `since`.

## Tests
Port the row tests from `tests/plugin.bats`; conformance cases `rows-*`.

Port `install.sh` and `uninstall.sh` to `asb install` / `asb uninstall [--purge]`. Idempotent.

## Install
- copy the running `asb` to `~/Library/Application Support/agentic-status-bar/bin/asb`;
- back up `~/.claude/settings.json` (`CLAUDE_STATUSBAR_SETTINGS` overrides) and add one async hook per event (`SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PreToolUse`, `PostToolUse`, `Notification`, `Stop`, `SubagentStart`, `SubagentStop`, `SessionEnd`) running `"'<stable path>' hook # agentic-status-bar"`, keeping all other hooks and key order;
- remove entries carrying the old `# swiftbar-claudecode-minimal` marker;
- refuse an invalid settings file;
- link the SwiftBar plugin while it exists (`CLAUDE_STATUSBAR_SWIFTBAR_DIR` or SwiftBar's `PluginDirectory`).

## Uninstall
Uninstall removes our hooks (and empty groups), the stable copy, the SwiftBar link and the login item; `--purge` also state and config, otherwise ask on a TTY.

## Tests
Port `tests/install.bats` to Swift tests on temp homes.

Each row gets a context menu (and a hover '…' button), plus an 'Unmute all projects' button.

## Row menu
- Mute project for 1 hour / for today, or Unmute project;
- Copy session ID;
- Copy working directory;
- Open folder in Finder;
- Reveal transcript;
- Focus (when in herdr).

## Details
- An 'Unmute all projects' button shows while mutes are active.
- Use the `ASBCore` action functions directly (not the CLI).
